8.1 Data compat with bookmark+
==============================

By design, bookmark-gt reads and writes alist entries under the same
keys bookmark+ uses so files round-trip both ways:

Key               Meaning
---------------------------------------------------
‘tags’            List of tag strings
‘bmkp-temp’       Temp-record marker
‘auto-update’     Auto-tracking flag
‘visits’          Visit count
‘last-visited’    Last visit timestamp
‘created’         Record creation timestamp
‘last-modified’   Record last-mutation timestamp

   Two shape differences we accommodate on read:

   • Bookmark+ writes the placeholder string ‘" - no file -"’ into
     ‘filename’ for non-file records.  ‘bookmark-gt-filename-of’ treats
     it as nil.  Bookmark-gt records omit ‘filename’ entirely for
     non-file records.
   • Bookmark+ URL records store the URL under ‘location’.  Bookmark-gt
     writes it under ‘url’.  Both are read by ‘bookmark-gt-url-of’.


File: bookmark-gt.info,  Node: Migrating from bookmark+,  Prev: Data compat with bookmark+,  Up: Compatibility

8.2 Migrating from bookmark+
============================

Records saved by bookmark+ carry handler symbols (‘bmkp-jump-dired’,
‘bmkp-jump-url-browse’, ‘bmkp-jump-url-browse-other-window’,
‘bmkp-gt-browsel-tabs-jump’) that are unbound when bookmark+ is not
loaded.  bookmark-gt registers these symbols as classification aliases
so the list buffer's Type column and the jump reader's narrow menu work
regardless — but jumping still calls ‘(funcall <symbol> record)’ and
fails when the function is not defined.

   Fix once with ‘bookmark-gt-migrate’:

     ;; One-time; not autoloaded — load explicitly.
     (require 'bookmark-gt-migrate)
     ;; Preview mutates `bookmark-alist' in memory only.
     (bookmark-gt-migrate-from-bookmark-plus)
     ;; Inspect via `M-x bookmark-gt-list' — verify the migrated
     ;; rows show the expected Type and jump correctly — then commit:
     (bookmark-save)

   What the migration does per record:

   • Rewrites the ‘handler’ symbol to the bookmark-gt equivalent.
   • For URL records, copies ‘location’ to ‘url’ (bookmark-gt's
     convention) and drops ‘location’.
   • Strips bookmark+ bookkeeping props that have no bookmark-gt
     meaning: ‘bmkp-gt-load-index’, ‘buffer-name’,
     ‘front-context-region-string’, ‘rear-context-region-string’, empty
     ‘annotation’, empty ‘tags’.
   • Preserves ‘filename’, ‘position’, ‘front-context-string’,
     ‘rear-context-string’, ‘visits’, ‘last-visited’, ‘created’,
     ‘last-modified’.
   • Preserves the Dired state keys ‘dired-directory’, ‘dired-marked’,
     ‘dired-subdirs’, ‘dired-hidden-dirs’, ‘dired-switches’ —
     bookmark-gt's Dired handler consumes them the same way bookmark+
     did.

   Records already in bookmark-gt form (or plain file bookmarks with a
nil handler) are left untouched.  Keep a copy of the bookmark file
before running.


